        <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" hidden>
        <div class="details-inner">
          <p class="answer"><strong>Cats are natural predators built for short bursts of energy,</strong> so they conserve power by resting a lot. Many healthy adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span>How can I help my cat stay entertained indoors?</span>
        <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" hidden>
        <div class="details-inner">
          <p class="answer"><strong>Offer a mix of climbing, scratching, and hunting-style play.</strong> Cat trees, puzzle feeders, wand toys, and window perches help indoor cats stay active, curious, and mentally engaged.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span>Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
        <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" hidden>
        <div class="details-inner">
          <p class="answer"><strong>Kneading is usually a comforting behavior</strong> that starts in kittenhood during nursing. Adult cats may knead soft blankets, beds, or laps when they feel relaxed and secure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
        <span>What does a slowly blinking cat mean?</span>
        <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
